    "created_at": "2021-04-28T18:00:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-04-28T18:00:08Z",
    "body": "I think the goal here is to provide a readable value. Are there any issues with having things like CJK characters in their decoded form (depending on underlying impl they may not be encoded in memory already) when piping through other APIs? Given things like:\r\n\r\n```mjs\r\n> new URL('./你好.js', 'https://example.test').href\r\n\"https://example.test/%E4%BD%A0%E5%A5%BD.js\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt seems like this could be a win for non-latin languages in terms of usability via readability / inspection.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
